 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Anchored in Tabuk (94:1-5). The oaths of 95-96 are framed («كاذبين معتذرين», «كذبًا»). 96 keeps Al-Muyassar's «ممن استمروا على الفسوق» (As-Sa'di: the door of repentance stays open). Geometric for «عالم الغيب والشهادة»; nothing drawn for the Fire (95). STAGING v4: c1 (94): a town by day. Three believers walk in from the left (returning: Al-Muyassar, from Tabuk; nothing of the expedition is drawn) and three men (the hypocrites who stayed behind) stand on the right and speak toward the believers on 94:2 (they make excuses to you, the believers: Al-Muyassar). The answer of 94:6-11 is the Messenger's («قل»): nobody acts it; the camera holds on the hypocrites; the shot is wide while the Messenger is named (94:17-20); a geometric plate on the Knower of the unseen (94:24-26); nothing is drawn for the return to Him. c2 (95-96): the same town. The hypocrites swear on 95:1 toward the believers (to you: both tafsirs); the shot is wide from 95:6 so the believers are in frame when they turn their backs on 95:9 (the command to them: Al-Muyassar, avoid them; As-Sa'di, no rebuke and no punishment, only turning away); during the threat and the Fire (95:11-18) the camera holds on the hypocrites, nothing is drawn for the Fire. They swear again on 96:1 toward the believers' turned backs; no plate in this chapter; nothing is acted on the conditional 96:5-7; the camera holds on the hypocrites for the end of the verse. The speech arcs point at the believers (renderer: arcs aim at the nearest person). Cover: the hypocrites making excuses (94:2)."
 },
